From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:20:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: program the full SM8475 init
 sequence for every gear

The SM8475 configuration keeps the PLL VCO/charge-pump values, the
MODE1 PLL settings, TX FR_DCC_CTRL, RX VGA_CAL_MAN_VAL and the PCS
PLL_CNTL and HS gear capabilities only in its HS-G4 overlay.
qmp_ufs_get_gear_overlay() applies that overlay only when the requested
PHY gear is G4, so a host limited to a lower gear (for example with
limit-hs-gear = <3>) leaves those registers at their reset values. The
table also lacks QSERDES_V6_COM_BG_TIMER.

Qualcomm's downstream cape (SM8475) PHY driver programs a single table
for both its G4 and non-G4 cases (phy_cal_table_rate_A and
phy_cal_table_rate_A_no_g4 are identical), including BG_TIMER = 0x0e.
Give SM8475 its own base serdes/tx/rx/pcs tables with those values and
drop the G4 overlay, as the Milos configuration already does. The values
programmed for G4 do not change apart from the added BG_TIMER; the
second-lane entries are covered by the per-lane tx/rx tables. Rate B
keeps VCO_TUNE_MAP = 0x44.

Upstream fixed the same class of problem for SM8650 in 81af9e40e2e4
("phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: Fix SM8650 PCS table for Gear 4") and SM8750 in
80305760d7a5 ("phy-qcom-qmp-ufs: Fix kaanapali PHY PLL lock failure
after SM8650 G4 fix").

Reference: LineageOS/android_kernel_qcom_sm8450 lineage-20
952aa00564cbb2cc788378c97e08958c4b889758,
drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-ufs-qmp-v4-cape.h

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c | 63 +++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
